dst_mmrs, dst_sink_mmrs: correct DST register descriptions

Several DST and DST sink MMR descriptions disagreed with the RTL, or
were empty where software needs them:

- trDstVendorStreamLength gave 32 * 2^(code + 1) frames. Codes 0 to 4
  select 32 to 512 frames, 32 << code, and codes 5 to 7 fall back to 32.
  The length applies only in stream-counting sync mode.
- trDstSyncMode called every value other than 2'b10 "NA". 2'b01 enables
  stream counting, 2'b10 sends periodic timestamps, and 2'b00 and 2'b11
  do neither.
- The packet header source ID comes from trDstInstFeatures[trDstSrcID]
  bits [3:0]; CDbgDebugTraceCfg[trace_source_id] is stored but never
  read.
- The producer pads frames to trDstVendorFrameLength * 64 bytes, but the
  sink finds frame boundaries at the power of two given by the highest
  set bit of its own frame length, so only 1, 2, 4 and 8 agree. The two
  frame-length fields now state that and that they must match.
- A read of trDstRamData launches a trace-RAM read and, when unread data
  is present, advances trDstRamRPLow by one 32-bit word, wrapping from
  the limit to the start. Neither field described this.

Recorded as a patch so the hand-mirrored upstream/ tree stays
reproducible from the vendored spec plus patches/ applied in order.
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_mmrs.yml
index fe1eef242..e6ceaecc0 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_mmrs.yml
@@ -140,8 +140,10 @@ trDstControl:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '17:16'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: When the field is set tp 2'b10, sent timestamp. All other vlaues
-      not NA.
+    DESCRIPTION: 'Periodic sync mode. 2''b00: off. 2''b01: stream counting, with
+      trDstVendorStreamLength frames between non-compressed packets. 2''b10: send
+      a timestamp packet every 2^(trDstSyncMax + 4) Cluster clocks. 2''b11: no
+      effect, as 2''b00.'
     HW_READ: DST
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
@@ -224,8 +226,11 @@ trDstImpl:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '27:24'
     RESET_VALUE: '1'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: Specify frame length. Frame Length = trDstVendorFrameLength* 64 ;
-      Frame Length should be a multiple of Bank Data Width.
+    DESCRIPTION: Specify frame length. Frame Length = trDstVendorFrameLength* 64 bytes;
+      Frame Length should be a multiple of Bank Data Width. Only 1, 2, 4 and 8 (64,
+      128, 256 and 512 bytes) are supported, because the DST sink finds frame boundaries
+      at the power of two given by the highest set bit of its frame length. Program
+      the sink's trDstRamVendorFrameLength with the same value.
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
@@ -235,8 +240,9 @@ trDstImpl:
     RESET_VALUE: '4'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
     DESCRIPTION: Specify Stream length. A stream starts with "no compressed packet".
-      Stream length specifies number of frames before a non-compressed packet is sent.Stream
-      Length = 32* 2^(trDstVendorStreamLength + 1)
+      Stream length specifies number of frames before a non-compressed packet is sent,
+      and applies only when trDstSyncMode is 2'b01. Values 0 to 4 give Stream Length
+      = 32* 2^trDstVendorStreamLength (32 to 512 frames); values 5 to 7 give 32.
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
@@ -289,7 +295,7 @@ trDstInstFeatures:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '27:16'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: ''
+    DESCRIPTION: Source ID sent in the trace packet headers. Only bits [3:0] are used.
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
@@ -364,7 +370,7 @@ c_dbg_debug_trace_cfg:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '3:0'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: 'Trace Source ID'
+    DESCRIPTION: Stored but not used. The trace packet headers carry trDstInstFeatures[trDstSrcID].
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
diff --git a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
index 7968c05a2..e6ab2de16 100644
--- a/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
+++ b/rtl/mmr/spec/dst_sink_mmrs.yml
@@ -112,7 +112,8 @@ trDstRamImpl:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '27:24'
     RESET_VALUE: '1'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: ''
+    DESCRIPTION: Frame length in 64-byte units. Only 1, 2, 4 and 8 (64, 128, 256 and
+      512 bytes) are supported, and the value must match the DST's trDstVendorFrameLength.
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
@@ -282,7 +283,9 @@ trDstRamRPLow:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '31:2'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: ''
+    DESCRIPTION: Read pointer, in 32-bit words; bits [31:2] of the byte address of
+      the word the next trDstRamData read returns. Each trDstRamData read that returns
+      unread data advances it by one word, and from trDstRamLimitLow it wraps to trDstRamStartLow.
     HW_WRITE: DST_SINK
     SW_WRITE: W
     SW_READ: R
@@ -333,7 +336,9 @@ trDstRamData:
     FIELDS_RANGE: '31:0'
     RESET_VALUE: '0'
     LEGAL_VALUE: ''
-    DESCRIPTION: ''
+    DESCRIPTION: Reading launches a trace-RAM read at trDstRamRPLow. When the RAM
+      holds unread data, the read returns that 32-bit word and advances trDstRamRPLow;
+      otherwise the pointer does not move.
     SW_READ: R
     SW_TYPE: ''
